        "original_id": "66ed2d17-218e-5a5b-a84d-27b8219c4363",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ælfgifu of Exeter, Ælfgifu of Shaftesbury, Edmund I, Eadwig, Edgar\n- Places: Exeter Cathedral, Shaftesbury\n- Roles: Anglo-Saxon saint, queen, king\n\nFacts:\n- Ælfgifu of Exeter was an Anglo-Saxon saint of unknown date and origin.\n- The relics of Ælfgifu of Exeter were held by Exeter Cathedral.\n- Ælfgifu of Shaftesbury, also known as Saint Elgiva, died in 944.\n- Ælfgifu of Shaftesbury was the first wife of Edmund I, who reigned from 939 to 946.\n- Ælfgifu of Shaftesbury and Edmund I had two sons who later became kings: Eadwig, who reigned from 955 to 959, and Edgar, who reigned from 959 to 975.",
